<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Resht</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1732">1732</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Treaties of Resht</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Resht was an agreement of 1732 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, by which Russia agreed to return parts of the Caspian provinces it had occupied after the collapse of Safavid power. It was negotiated while Nader was restoring Iranian authority. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> cite it, together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ganja">Treaty of Ganja</a> of 1735, as part of Nader's recovery of Iranian territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-resht.jpg" alt="Treaty of Resht" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Robert Shepherd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shepherd-c-138-139.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
